{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "name": "Avena data quality",
  "built_at": "2026-11-11T23:44:54.155Z",
  "series_start": "2026-08-05",
  "method": "Daily capture counts are the days in the observation ledger published with the open dataset. That ledger counts listing rows in Avena's price snapshots from 2026-08-05. A calendar day in that span with no row is missing. Its listing count is left blank. Nothing is interpolated. The declared capture gap is 2026-10-14 to 2026-10-20. Field completeness and coverage by province and town are counted on the current committed listing book, the book the site serves. Weekly new listings and delistings are the public absorption series from the same daily snapshots. A delisting is a listing reference that was seen and is absent from the latest snapshot. It is not a confirmed sale. Same-unit figures compare closed-week copies of the listing book, the same captures as the weekly vintages and the same-unit asking-price index. A price change counts only when that index's unit-identity check calls it the same unit: property type, bedrooms and bathrooms equal, and built and plot size within 2%. A change of 25% or more also needs full specs on both sides, the same photo set, a new EUR per square metre inside the area band, and a price that does not return exactly to an earlier asking price of that reference on this weekly series within 365 days. A specification change is excluded. A large change that fails the check is held back. A step that crosses the declared gap is the change between the two captures that exist. It is not split across the missing days. The listing record has no brochure or developer-PDF field. A PDF link is counted only when the listing URL itself is an http or https address ending in .pdf.",
  "caveats": [
    "The trusted daily series starts on 2026-08-05. Earlier stored rows repeated a frozen book and are not included. The history is short.",
    "Figures are asking prices of listings. A listing reference on a new-build is often a unit type in a development, not one dwelling.",
    "A delisting means the reference left the captured feed. It may have sold or it may have been withdrawn. It is not a confirmed sale.",
    "Same-unit counts are weekly comparisons of closed-week listing files. They are not every daily price change. The open dataset moves file contains only changes that passed the same-unit check, so it cannot be the denominator of a pass share.",
    "A change below 25% is accepted when a specification field is missing on one side. A change of 25% or more is held back when a required spec is missing.",
    "Days inside a declared capture gap have no listing count. No day is filled in from another day.",
    "Some days have a price snapshot and no commit of the listing file. Those days are listed under feed-file gaps. They are not missing snapshots.",
    "Plot size is often absent. A missing plot is absent, not zero square metres.",
    "The current week is not in the same-unit comparison until that week is closed and frozen."
  ],
